WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.400 --> 00:00:02.634
-Welcome back to the show, Zoe.
-Thank you.

00:00:02.634 --> 00:00:04.467
-Who can be hotter
than you right now?

00:00:04.467 --> 00:00:06.400
We have things I got
to talk to you about.

00:00:06.400 --> 00:00:08.467
So many things.
I'm so happy for you.

00:00:08.467 --> 00:00:09.968
-Aww, thanks.
-But you're busy, busy, busy.

00:00:09.968 --> 00:00:11.901
-I'm a busy bee.
-Yeah.

00:00:11.901 --> 00:00:14.267
"Beau Is Afraid"
is out tomorrow.

00:00:14.267 --> 00:00:16.834
This is -- Yeah,
already everyone...

00:00:16.834 --> 00:00:18.767
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:18.767 --> 00:00:20.934
The poster came out online,

00:00:20.934 --> 00:00:22.801
and it went viral
just from the poster.

00:00:22.801 --> 00:00:24.367
-Yeah. It's insane.

00:00:24.367 --> 00:00:26.534
-It's Ari Aster?
-Ari Aster --

00:00:26.534 --> 00:00:29.133
I think, one of the great
filmmakers of our time.

00:00:29.133 --> 00:00:31.400
You know, "Hereditary,"
"Midsommar."

00:00:31.400 --> 00:00:35.767
Now, this is his, like,
epic dark comedy.

00:00:35.767 --> 00:00:38.601
-What is it about?
-He describes it

00:00:38.601 --> 00:00:42.000
as a Jewish "Lord of the Rings."
[ Laughter ]

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:45.000
Which people have also
described me as.

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:46.567
[ Laughter ]
Which is strange.

00:00:46.567 --> 00:00:49.634
It's like -- It's
a three-hour-long

00:00:49.634 --> 00:00:51.501
nightmare comedy.
Am I selling it well?

00:00:51.501 --> 00:00:53.100
-Yeah, so far.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:53.100 --> 00:00:55.300
-And it stars Joaquin Phoenix.
-Yes.

00:00:55.300 --> 00:00:58.200
-I play
Joaquin Phoenix' mother.

00:00:58.200 --> 00:01:01.334
So I guess I'm in
that stage of my career.

00:01:01.334 --> 00:01:02.801
[ Laughter ]

00:01:02.801 --> 00:01:04.601
I play her young.
-Okay, good. That makes sense.

00:01:04.601 --> 00:01:07.033
-I play a young Patti LuPone,
which is...

00:01:07.033 --> 00:01:08.467
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:08.467 --> 00:01:10.133
Yeah.
-That's pressure there.

00:01:10.133 --> 00:01:13.133
Did you guys get together
and try to act like...

00:01:13.133 --> 00:01:15.000
-Yeah, I had to --
I had to study Patti,

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:17.968
which is like, you know,
any -- any actor's dream.

00:01:17.968 --> 00:01:21.033
She's like --
Yeah, she's amazing.

00:01:21.033 --> 00:01:22.901
-Phenomenal.
-She's so -- so singular.

00:01:22.901 --> 00:01:28.801
She does, like, a lot of really
intense mouth -- mouth acting,

00:01:28.801 --> 00:01:30.534
which I had to --
it's almost like Elvis.

00:01:30.534 --> 00:01:31.968
Like, there's a lot of,
like, um, like...

00:01:31.968 --> 00:01:35.167
-She does do that.
-There's, like, a snarl.

00:01:35.167 --> 00:01:38.400
And then she -- and she sort of
talks in the back of her mouth

00:01:38.400 --> 00:01:40.734
and...
-That's so Patti LuPone.

00:01:40.734 --> 00:01:42.901
-It's not -- It's not great.
-That's a fantastic one.

00:01:42.901 --> 00:01:44.601
-It's like she's, um...
-I've never seen anyone do that.

00:01:44.601 --> 00:01:47.634
-She's almost, um, chewing,
you know.

00:01:47.634 --> 00:01:51.000
-Wow. That is
an amazing impression.

00:01:51.000 --> 00:01:52.334
I've never seen anyone
do that before.

00:01:52.334 --> 00:01:53.734
-[ Laughs ]
-That is so Patti LuPone.

00:01:53.734 --> 00:01:54.834
I love that.
-Thank you.

00:01:54.834 --> 00:01:56.501
-A little Elvis.
-It's a little Elvis.

00:01:56.501 --> 00:01:59.701
Yeah, I'm a little rusty, but --
But, no, we had so much fun.

00:01:59.701 --> 00:02:01.100
-You have that,

00:02:01.100 --> 00:02:03.234
but then also then
talk to me about "Slip."

00:02:03.234 --> 00:02:05.534
-Oh, man. Well, it's my baby.

00:02:05.534 --> 00:02:07.234
-You wrote this,
you directed this,

00:02:07.234 --> 00:02:09.033
you're in this.
I mean, wow, buddy.

00:02:09.033 --> 00:02:11.067
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Thanks.

00:02:11.067 --> 00:02:13.467
-It's on the Roku Channel.
-Yes.

00:02:13.467 --> 00:02:15.467
-Tomorrow. It's called "Slip."

00:02:15.467 --> 00:02:17.767
How did you get into it?

00:02:17.767 --> 00:02:19.467
What is it about?
What do we have things...

00:02:19.467 --> 00:02:21.701
Because it's a story I can't
really explain to people.

00:02:21.701 --> 00:02:23.267
-[ Laughs ] Yeah.

00:02:23.267 --> 00:02:25.067
-Only you could come up with
something like this.

00:02:25.067 --> 00:02:29.501
-It follows a character named
Mae, played by yours truly.

00:02:29.501 --> 00:02:33.234
And when we meet her,
she's feeling sort of stuck

00:02:33.234 --> 00:02:34.801
in her marriage, restless.

00:02:34.801 --> 00:02:37.567
And one night, she ends up
cheating on her husband

00:02:37.567 --> 00:02:39.767
and then wakes up
the next morning to discover

00:02:39.767 --> 00:02:41.400
that she's now married
to the guy

00:02:41.400 --> 00:02:42.901
she cheated
on her husband with.

00:02:42.901 --> 00:02:45.734
And over the course
of the season,

00:02:45.734 --> 00:02:48.033
she realizes
that through orgasm,

00:02:48.033 --> 00:02:50.534
she's being transported
into a multiverse.

00:02:50.534 --> 00:02:53.033
So, just...
[ Laughter ]

00:02:53.033 --> 00:02:55.367
[ Applause ]
-Whoa.

00:02:55.367 --> 00:02:59.267
-Yeah.
-W-Wow.

00:02:59.267 --> 00:03:02.634
So, how do you think
of an idea like this?

00:03:02.634 --> 00:03:06.501
How does the idea --
Can you walk me...

00:03:06.501 --> 00:03:08.434
-I'll walk you through it,
Jimmy.

00:03:08.434 --> 00:03:09.801
[ Laughter ]

00:03:09.801 --> 00:03:12.601
Well, um, I'm, like,
the type of person,

00:03:12.601 --> 00:03:14.634
like anyone I meet

00:03:14.634 --> 00:03:16.701
who I'm even
just moderately attracted to,

00:03:16.701 --> 00:03:19.300
I, like, flash-forward
to just a whole-ass life with.

00:03:19.300 --> 00:03:20.934
Do you know what I mean?
You know what I mean?

00:03:20.934 --> 00:03:22.334
[ Laughing ]

00:03:22.334 --> 00:03:24.667
-Do you see someone, you go,
"Hey, I see in the future"?

00:03:24.667 --> 00:03:27.100
-Yes, like, you know,
like, when you and I

00:03:27.100 --> 00:03:30.000
first met, years ago,
you know, I was like --

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:32.334
You just said hello.
I -- Yeah, I saw --

00:03:32.334 --> 00:03:35.367
I saw a life and, um...
[ Laughter ]

00:03:35.367 --> 00:03:38.267
Well, [Chuckles], and
it's a "Sliding Doors" thing.

00:03:38.267 --> 00:03:41.234
You know, like, I did -- I saw
a wholesome life,

00:03:41.234 --> 00:03:44.200
sort of maybe --
maybe like a Wyoming.

00:03:44.200 --> 00:03:46.334
Maybe we're running
an organic dairy farm.

00:03:46.334 --> 00:03:47.801
I, like...
-Me and you?

00:03:47.801 --> 00:03:49.200
-We're out of the business?
Yeah.

00:03:49.200 --> 00:03:51.300
We're agriculturally-minded
people.

00:03:51.300 --> 00:03:53.834
We have no children.
That's what I'm talking about.

00:03:53.834 --> 00:03:55.000
Me and you, Jimmy. Yeah.

00:03:55.000 --> 00:03:58.167
Like, no kids,
but, you know, cows and...

00:03:58.167 --> 00:03:59.501
[ Laughter ]

00:03:59.501 --> 00:04:01.133
-We started
a dairy farm together?

00:04:01.133 --> 00:04:04.467
-Yeah. Organic, though.
And that, I think --

00:04:04.467 --> 00:04:06.200
And, like,
that's always, like...

00:04:06.200 --> 00:04:07.934
I'm obsessed with,
like, the what-ifs.

00:04:07.934 --> 00:04:09.467
Do you know what I mean?
Like the "Sliding Doors."

00:04:09.467 --> 00:04:12.133
Like, you and I could be here,

00:04:12.133 --> 00:04:14.300
you know, you doing
whatever this is,

00:04:14.300 --> 00:04:16.400
and me doing...
[ Laughter ]

00:04:16.400 --> 00:04:19.667
-The job.
-It's a job, it's a job.

00:04:19.667 --> 00:04:21.534
Yeah, it's a job.
-Yeah.

00:04:21.534 --> 00:04:23.634
-And -- And me doing what I do.

00:04:23.634 --> 00:04:27.701
And -- Or, you know,
we could have just been just...

00:04:27.701 --> 00:04:30.868
-Yeah, yeah, we could have
been farmers, yeah.

00:04:30.868 --> 00:04:32.767
-Is that how you do it?
Is that how you do it?

00:04:32.767 --> 00:04:35.601
-Yes, of course.
-I've never milked a cow.

00:04:35.601 --> 00:04:37.634
-No, that's exactly right.
Yeah, it's good.

00:04:37.634 --> 00:04:39.367
-I'm going to stop doing that.
-Yeah, please, yeah.

00:04:39.367 --> 00:04:41.400
You're this close
to being a meme.

00:04:41.400 --> 00:04:43.501
[ Laughter ]

00:04:43.501 --> 00:04:45.000
Last time you were on the show,

00:04:45.000 --> 00:04:47.234
we talked about your love
for Timothée Chalamet,

00:04:47.234 --> 00:04:50.133
and we both share
our love for Timothée Chalamet.

00:04:50.133 --> 00:04:52.300
-Yeah, it's slightly different.
-A little different.

00:04:52.300 --> 00:04:56.167
I picture Timothée and I
as dairy farmers in the future,

00:04:56.167 --> 00:04:58.467
but I couldn't help
but mention --

00:04:58.467 --> 00:05:01.834
I couldn't help but notice
that in the first episode,

00:05:01.834 --> 00:05:04.167
you mentioned Timothée Chalamet,
and I was going to

00:05:04.167 --> 00:05:05.968
ask you about that.
I think he might be in the first

00:05:05.968 --> 00:05:07.601
two episodes,
you talked about him.

00:05:07.601 --> 00:05:10.434
-Yeah, he's sort of
constantly mentioned throughout.

00:05:10.434 --> 00:05:13.067
And it's -- I mean,
look, it's not great.

00:05:13.067 --> 00:05:16.400
Like I -- you know,
in my last movie, "How It Ends,"

00:05:16.400 --> 00:05:17.901
Olivia Wilde and I
were in a scene

00:05:17.901 --> 00:05:20.868
in which she told me
that in the afterlife,

00:05:20.868 --> 00:05:24.000
my character would be,
you know, shtupping Chalamet.

00:05:24.000 --> 00:05:28.834
And now, in this,
I literally am, like,

00:05:28.834 --> 00:05:31.501
invoking his name during climax.

00:05:31.501 --> 00:05:33.033
It's like -- It's a problem.
Like, I --

00:05:33.033 --> 00:05:34.467
-Yeah.
-It's troubling.

00:05:34.467 --> 00:05:36.501
It should be troubling for him.
I'm sure it's troubling

00:05:36.501 --> 00:05:39.601
to his team and loved ones,
friends and family.

00:05:39.601 --> 00:05:41.501
It's troubling to me.
-It is, yeah.

00:05:41.501 --> 00:05:42.934
Have you ever met
Timothée Chalamet?

00:05:42.934 --> 00:05:46.100
-Um, well, yes, I have.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:46.100 --> 00:05:49.601
-Does he know that you have
a little obsession?

00:05:49.601 --> 00:05:52.300
-I think he's aware. Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:52.300 --> 00:05:54.334
He -- Last time I saw him,

00:05:54.334 --> 00:05:56.300
it was at
the Venice Film Festival.

00:05:56.300 --> 00:06:00.667
And "How It Ends" had come out.

00:06:00.667 --> 00:06:04.000
So he was also aware,
um, of that scene.

00:06:04.000 --> 00:06:07.834
And I was, like, standing
across the room from him.

00:06:07.834 --> 00:06:12.334
And when he noticed me,
I saw his face sort of fall.

00:06:12.334 --> 00:06:14.234
[ Laughter ]

00:06:14.234 --> 00:06:15.734
-He was bummed out?

00:06:15.734 --> 00:06:17.067
-No, it was -- It was somewhere

00:06:17.067 --> 00:06:19.767
between, like, excitement
and sheer terror.

00:06:19.767 --> 00:06:21.000
[ Laughter ]

00:06:21.000 --> 00:06:22.701
But then we had
a mutual friend,

00:06:22.701 --> 00:06:24.434
and she, like,
sort of brought me over.

00:06:24.434 --> 00:06:26.701
But before she could
even introduce me,

00:06:26.701 --> 00:06:28.300
he was like, "Oh, snap."

00:06:28.300 --> 00:06:30.133
Like, he was -- Like, he knew.

00:06:30.133 --> 00:06:31.334
Was that a good Chalamet?

00:06:31.334 --> 00:06:33.100
-It was a, uh...
-"Snap."

00:06:33.100 --> 00:06:35.200
And then - And then...

00:06:35.200 --> 00:06:36.701
-That was another
good impression.

00:06:36.701 --> 00:06:39.834
-Thank you.
And then he, like, hugged me

00:06:39.834 --> 00:06:41.267
and then he sort of
took me in

00:06:41.267 --> 00:06:43.300
and was like,
"I thought you were taller."

00:06:43.300 --> 00:06:45.901
[ Laughter ]

00:06:45.901 --> 00:06:49.934
-Yeah, a classic Timo neg,
you know?

00:06:49.934 --> 00:06:52.968
Like -- But that's sort of
the way to my heart,

00:06:52.968 --> 00:06:55.334
you know, is
to just foster insecurity

00:06:55.334 --> 00:06:57.434
on...
[ Laughter ]

00:06:57.434 --> 00:06:58.801
-But it's interesting
that he knows you

00:06:58.801 --> 00:07:00.400
and knows and thought
about your height.

00:07:00.400 --> 00:07:02.467
-Well, that is really
the thing is, like,

00:07:02.467 --> 00:07:05.467
at first, I was like,
you know, "Ouch."

00:07:05.467 --> 00:07:07.534
But then later, I was like,

00:07:07.534 --> 00:07:09.200
"Yeah, he thought
about my height," like...

00:07:09.200 --> 00:07:11.300
[ Laughter ]
-Timothée Chalamet

00:07:11.300 --> 00:07:12.834
goes to bed at night
thinking about

00:07:12.834 --> 00:07:15.200
how tall Zoe Lister-Jones is.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:15.200 --> 00:07:18.000
-[ Laughs ]

00:07:18.000 --> 00:07:20.834
-Congrats on the series.
I want to show everyone a clip.

00:07:20.834 --> 00:07:23.033
Here is Zoe Lister-Jones
in "Slip."

00:07:23.033 --> 00:07:24.501
Take a look at this.

00:07:24.501 --> 00:07:29.400
-Sleeping to find meaning,
and waking to lose it.

00:07:29.400 --> 00:07:34.467
And all you want to do is sleep,

00:07:34.467 --> 00:07:36.767
to dream of something more.

00:07:36.767 --> 00:07:39.934
More.

00:07:39.934 --> 00:07:42.634
Just...

00:07:42.634 --> 00:07:45.601
-♪ Dream, baby, dream, baby,
dream, baby, dream, baby ♪

00:07:45.601 --> 00:07:48.434
-...more.

00:07:48.434 --> 00:07:52.300
-Yeah, um, I was just asking
how you're doing

00:07:52.300 --> 00:07:55.000
as, like, more of a courtesy.

00:07:55.000 --> 00:07:58.367
-Oh. Right. Yeah.

00:07:58.367 --> 00:08:00.567
-I mean, you do genuinely
sound [Bleep]-up.

00:08:00.567 --> 00:08:04.200
-Thank you. Thanks.
-But I'm literally 24.

00:08:04.200 --> 00:08:07.868
-Wow. That's a whole life ahead.
Exciting.

00:08:07.868 --> 00:08:10.567
-Yeah, "I wasn't really asking."
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:10.567 --> 00:08:12.200
Zoe Lister-Jones, everybody!

00:08:12.200 --> 00:08:15.868
All episodes of "Slip" are
available tomorrow

00:08:15.868 --> 00:08:17.968
on the Roku Channel.
More "Tonight Show"

00:08:17.968 --> 00:08:19.634
after the break.
Stick around.

